TITLE:: PianoRollNote
SUMMARY:: One recorded note in the piano roll with selection, part assignment, and grid editing.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PlayableNote, Classes/Event, Classes/AddCommand, Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/DeleteCommand, Classes/DragCommand, Classes/LeftCommand, Classes/LegatoCommand, Classes/PartCommand, Classes/RightCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollNote:: wraps a LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: and a LINK::Classes/Event:: with piano-roll UI callbacks (view creation, selection highlighting, part colours, view repositioning after timing edits, and deletion). Commands such as LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: and LINK::Classes/LegatoCommand:: write keys onto the composed LINK::Classes/Event:: (for example CODE::\amp::, CODE::\legato::) and keep the LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: in sync. LINK::Classes/DeleteCommand:: calls LINK::#-delete::, which removes the note view and runs the optional delete callback. LINK::Classes/LeftCommand:: and LINK::Classes/RightCommand:: call LINK::#-nudgeLeft:: and LINK::#-nudgeRight::. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: creates an instance on note-on and LINK::Classes/AddCommand:: inserts that same note on note-off.

NOTE::
You can run the unit tests for TELETYPE::PianoRollNote:: by running:
CODE::
(
UnitTest.reportPasses_(false);
PianoRollNoteUnitTests.run;
)
::
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollNote::.

ARGUMENT:: startTime
Note-on time in beats.

ARGUMENT:: noteNumber
MIDI note number.

ARGUMENT:: velocity
MIDI velocity.

ARGUMENT:: viewFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called from LINK::#-stop:: to create the note's LINK::Classes/View::.

ARGUMENT:: selectFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called when the note becomes selected, with the note view and this note. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: paints the border LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2::.

ARGUMENT:: deselectFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called when the note is deselected, with the note view and this note. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: restores the part colour on the border.

ARGUMENT:: paintFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called with the note view when the part or the amplitude changes and the view exists. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: uses it to paint the part colour.

ARGUMENT:: moveFunc
LINK::Classes/Function:: called after timing edits with CODE::func.value(view, startTime, stopTime)::.

ARGUMENT:: deleteFunc
Optional LINK::Classes/Function:: called from LINK::#-delete:: with the note as its argument. CODE::nil:: is allowed. The callback is kept, so a restored note can be deleted again. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: uses this callback to drop the note from the roll and update playback.

ARGUMENT:: insertFunc
Optional LINK::Classes/Function:: called with the note when LINK::#-restoreAmplitudeImage:: puts a deleted note back. CODE::nil:: is allowed. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: uses this callback to return the note to the roll.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: amp_
Clips CODE::value:: to CODE::0::–CODE::1::. A clipped value of CODE::0:: calls LINK::#-delete:: and does not write the event or the velocity. Any value above CODE::0:: stores it as CODE::\amp:: on the composed LINK::Classes/Event:: and passes the clipped value to LINK::Classes/PlayableNote#-amp_::, which sets the MIDI velocity. A tiny positive value stays a note even when that velocity rounds to CODE::0::. When the note view exists, CODE::paintFunc:: is called so the roll can redraw the fill and the border. LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: calls this method, so that opacity updates. The roll chooses the part colour, wrapping LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour1:: through LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5::. An unselected note's border is that colour at full opacity. A selected note's border stays LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2::. The fill uses the same colour at this amplitude as opacity.

ARGUMENT:: value
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: amplitude. Values outside CODE::0:: to CODE::1:: are clipped silently.

METHOD:: amplitudeImage
The amplitude undo snapshot: CODE::\amp:: (CODE::nil:: when the event has no amplitude), CODE::\velocity::, and CODE::\deleted::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event::.

METHOD:: amplitudeImageIfChanged
The current LINK::#-amplitudeImage:: when CODE::value:: would change this note, or CODE::nil:: when it would not. A clipped value of CODE::0:: changes a note that is still in the roll. A positive value changes a note whose event amplitude or mapped velocity differs. LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: uses this to skip notes that are already at the target.

ARGUMENT:: value
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: amplitude, clipped the same way as LINK::#-amp_::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: assignPart
Stores CODE::partNumber:: on the wrapped LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: and, when the note view exists, calls CODE::paintFunc:: with that view. LINK::Classes/PartCommand:: calls this method.

ARGUMENT:: partNumber
An LINK::Classes/Integer:: part number.

METHOD:: delete
Removes the note view, marks the note as not inserted, clears selection without running the deselect callback, and calls CODE::deleteFunc:: once with this note. The callback is kept. A second call while the note is already deleted does nothing. A later LINK::#-stop:: does not recreate the view. LINK::#-restoreAmplitudeImage:: can put the note back.

METHOD:: deselect
Clears selection and invokes the deselect callback.

METHOD:: ensureView
Creates the note view when this note is not deleted, has no view yet, and either has a stop time or already had view bounds. Does nothing otherwise. LINK::#-stop:: schedules this. LINK::Classes/AddCommand#-restore:: calls it when putting the note back.

METHOD:: event
The composed LINK::Classes/Event::, created with no parent so default pattern keys such as CODE::\amp:: are unset until a command writes them.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event::.

METHOD:: insert
Marks the note inserted and calls CODE::insertFunc:: once with this note. Does not create the view. A second call does nothing. LINK::Classes/AddCommand#-execute:: calls this.

METHOD:: isDeleted
Returns whether LINK::#-delete:: has removed this note and it has not been restored.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: isInserted
Returns whether LINK::#-insert:: has put this note in the roll and LINK::#-delete:: has not since removed it.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: isSelected
Returns whether this note is currently selected.

METHOD:: legatoImage
The legato undo snapshot: CODE::\legato:: (CODE::nil:: when the event has no legato) and CODE::\stopTime::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event::.

METHOD:: legatoImageIfChanged
The current LINK::#-legatoImage:: when CODE::value:: and CODE::nextOnset:: would change this note, or CODE::nil:: when the event already stores that legato and the stop time already matches CODE::startTime + (nextOnset - startTime) * value::.

ARGUMENT:: value
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: legato greater than CODE::0::.

ARGUMENT:: nextOnset
The beat LINK::#-legato_:: would use as the next onset.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: legato_
Stores CODE::value:: as CODE::\legato:: on the composed LINK::Classes/Event:: with no clipping or mapping, then sets the wrapped LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: stop time via LINK::Classes/PlayableNote#-applyLegato::. Repositions the note view when it exists.

ARGUMENT:: value
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber:: legato greater than CODE::0::. Values greater than CODE::1:: are allowed.

ARGUMENT:: nextOnsetTime
The beat of the next distinct onset, or the loop end for the last note group.

METHOD:: moveTo
Places the note at CODE::startTime:: and CODE::noteNumber::. Duration is preserved. The start time is clamped at beat zero. The MIDI note number is clamped to CODE::0::–CODE::127::. When the note view exists, it is moved to the new time and pitch.

ARGUMENT:: startTime
Note-on time in beats. A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::. Values below CODE::0:: are clamped to CODE::0::.

ARGUMENT:: noteNumber
MIDI note number. An LINK::Classes/Integer::. Values outside CODE::0:: to CODE::127:: are clamped.

METHOD:: noteNumber
Returns the wrapped note's MIDI note number.

METHOD:: nudgeLeft
Moves the note one grid step left at CODE::resolution:: beats. If the start time is already on the grid, subtracts one step; if off-grid, moves to the adjacent grid line to the left. Preserves duration; start time is clamped at beat zero.

ARGUMENT:: resolution
Grid spacing in beats (for example CODE::0.125:: for sixteenth notes in a quarter-note grid).

METHOD:: nudgeRight
Moves the note one grid step right at CODE::resolution:: beats. If the start time is already on the grid, adds one step; if off-grid, moves to the adjacent grid line to the right. Preserves duration; start time is clamped at beat zero.

ARGUMENT:: resolution
Grid spacing in beats.

METHOD:: partNumber
The part stored on the wrapped LINK::Classes/PlayableNote::. New notes are part 1. LINK::#-assignPart:: changes it. The roll uses that number for the note colour, and LINK::Classes/WriteCommand:: uses it to group the pattern.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Integer::.

METHOD:: playableNote
Returns the wrapped LINK::Classes/PlayableNote::.

METHOD:: refreshView
Repositions the note view from its current start and stop times using the piano roll's current horizontal scale. Does nothing when the view has not been created yet.

METHOD:: restoreAmplitudeImage
Writes an amplitude snapshot from LINK::#-amplitudeImage:: back onto this note. A snapshot with CODE::\deleted:: true deletes the note. Otherwise a deleted note is put back: CODE::insertFunc:: runs, and the view is created again when one had already existed. CODE::\amp:: is removed when the snapshot's amplitude is CODE::nil::, and the stored velocity is written back.

ARGUMENT:: image
An LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\amp::, CODE::\velocity::, and CODE::\deleted::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: restoreLegatoImage
Writes a legato snapshot back onto this note. CODE::\legato:: is removed when the snapshot's legato is CODE::nil::. CODE::\stopTime:: is written back, and CODE::moveFunc:: is called when the note view exists and the stop time changes. LINK::Classes/LegatoCommand:: calls this method.

ARGUMENT:: image
An LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\legato:: and CODE::\stopTime::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: restoreTimeImage
Writes CODE::\startTime:: and CODE::\stopTime:: from a time snapshot back onto this note. When the note view exists, CODE::moveFunc:: is called with the restored times. LINK::Classes/LeftCommand::, LINK::Classes/RightCommand::, and LINK::Classes/SnapCommand:: call this method.

ARGUMENT:: image
An LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\startTime:: and CODE::\stopTime::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: selectIfEnclosed
Selects or deselects based on whether this note's view lies inside CODE::possiblyEnclosingView::.

ARGUMENT:: possiblyEnclosingView
A LINK::Classes/View:: whose bounds define the selection rectangle.

ARGUMENT:: addToExistingSelection
When true, notes outside the rectangle are left unchanged; when false, they are deselected.

METHOD:: snapToGrid
Snaps the start time to the nearest grid line at CODE::resolution:: beats and shifts the stop time by the same delta so duration is preserved. Start time is clamped at beat zero.

ARGUMENT:: resolution
Grid spacing in beats.

METHOD:: startTime
Returns the note-on time in beats.

METHOD:: stop
Sets the note-off time and schedules creation of the note view. The scheduled creation does nothing when the note has been deleted or the view already exists.

ARGUMENT:: stopTime
Note-off time in beats.

METHOD:: stopTime
Returns the note-off time in beats.

METHOD:: timeImage
The start and stop time currently stored on this note.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\startTime:: and CODE::\stopTime::.

METHOD:: timeImageIfNudged
The current LINK::#-timeImage:: when a nudge by CODE::spacing:: in CODE::direction:: would move the start time, or CODE::nil:: when the start would stay put. CODE::direction:: is CODE::-1:: for left and CODE::1:: for right. LINK::Classes/LeftCommand:: and LINK::Classes/RightCommand:: use this to skip notes that are already at the destination, including a left nudge clamped at beat zero.

ARGUMENT:: spacing
The grid step in beats.

ARGUMENT:: direction
CODE::-1:: to try a left nudge, or CODE::1:: to try a right nudge.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: timeImageIfSnapped
The current LINK::#-timeImage:: when snapping to CODE::spacing:: would move the start time, or CODE::nil:: when the start is already on that grid. LINK::Classes/SnapCommand:: uses this to skip notes that would not move.

ARGUMENT:: spacing
The grid step in beats.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Event::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: toggleSelect
Toggles selection and runs the select or deselect callback.

METHOD:: transpose
Adds CODE::semitones:: to the MIDI note number. When the note view exists, moves it vertically by that many rows. Positive values raise the note.

ARGUMENT:: semitones
An LINK::Classes/Integer::. Negative values lower the note.

METHOD:: velocity
Returns the wrapped note's velocity.

PRIVATE:: init, prApplyPartColour, prApplyTimeDelta, prIsOnGrid, prStartAfterNudge, prStartAfterSnap, prUndelete
